{{Quote|The Time Variance Authority. We're really a watchdog organization. Except we're more lighthearted than that sounds with a sort of throwback ironic twist. And we're in charge of defending what's known as the [[Sacred Timeline]].|[[Mr. Paradox]] to [[Deadpool]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
The '''Time Variance Authority''' ('''TVA''') is a bureaucratic organization created by [[He Who Remains]] and located outside of time and space that originally served as a temporal law enforcement agency, tasked with preserving the [[Sacred Timeline]] by preventing the creation of alternate timelines. Following [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]]'s decision to destroy the [[Temporal Loom]] and allow the [[Multiverse]] to flourish, the TVA shifted its focus to monitoring the Multiverse and tracking down [[Hub:Victor Timely|Variants]] of He Who Remains.

==History==
===Foundation===
====True Foundation====
{{Quote|Eons ago, before the TVA, a Variant of myself lived on [[Earth]] in the 31st century. He was a scientist and he discovered that there were universes stacked on top of his own.|[[He Who Remains]]|For All Time. Always.}}
Eons ago, a Variant of [[He Who Remains]] lived on [[Earth]] in the 31st century. One day, he discovered the existence of alternate universes that were stacked on top of each other. At the same time, other Variants of himself were learning the same thing, leading them to eventually make contact with one another. The Variants shared knowledge and technologies from their respective universes to improve the others. However, certain nefarious Variants saw the new universes as new lands to conquer, leading to a [[Multiversal War]]. The Variants battled each other to preserve their universe and annihilate the others. At one point, He Who Remains encountered [[Alioth]], a creature created from the several tears in reality with the ability to consume time and space itself. He weaponized Alioth's power to put an end to the Multiversal War before isolating the [[Sacred Timeline]] and creating the Time Variance Authority to manage the flow of time and prevent any alternate timelines.{{Ref|LK106}} He recruited Variants to work for him,{{Ref|LK103}} with [[Ravonna Renslayer]] as his general and trusted second-in-command. Upon reaching an era of peace, He Who Remains ordered [[Miss Minutes]] to wipe every TVA personnel's memories of him before making them believe that they were created by the [[Time-Keepers]] to protect the Sacred Timeline.{{Ref|LK204}}

====Visited by Loki====
A [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Variant]] of [[Loki]] was blasted through a [[Timedoor]] into the TVA's [[Time Variance Authority Office|office]] and rushed to find [[Mobius M. Mobius]] and [[Hunter B-15]], claiming that [[He Who Remains|someone]] was coming. However, Mobius and B-15 had no memory of Loki,{{Ref|LK106}} and eventually realized that he was a Variant, prompting them to chase him alongside several [[Minutemen]]. Loki pled with Mobius, who did not remember him, so Loki jumped off the ledge into a [[Time Variance Authority Mail Cart|mail cart]], which crashed into another room. Loki assured everyone that it was alright as the mail cart left and asked if [[Casey]] remembered him while the TVA sent out a notice about Loki fleeing to all personnel. Casey called out that he had found the intruder, but Loki then [[Time Slipping|time slipped]] away.{{Ref|LK201}}

====Discussing Time Slipping====
[[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] [[Time Slipping|time slipped]] in front of [[Ouroboros]] and asked how he would be able to fix his time slipping. Ouroboros first insisted that it was impossible to time slip in the [[Time Variance Authority Office]], so Loki phrased the question as a hypothetical. Ouroboros told Loki that someone at the time period he wanted to be in would have to use a [[Temporal Aura Extractor]] while Loki pruned himself. Loki had Ouroboros make and hold onto an extractor, when he suddenly time slipped back to his present.{{Ref|LK201}}

====TVA Propaganda====
[[File:Reorganizing the Multiverse.png|{{AltFloat}}|The [[Time-Keepers]] restructure the [[Multiverse]]]]
{{Quote|Long ago, there was a vast [[Multiversal War]]. Countless unique timelines battled each other for supremacy, nearly resulting in the total destruction of... well, everything. But then, the all-knowing [[Time-Keepers]] emerged, bringing peace by reorganizing the multiverse into a single timeline, the Sacred Timeline.|[[Miss Minutes]]|Glorious Purpose (Loki Season One)}}
The Time Variance Authority propaganda told of countless timelines battling one another for dominance across the [[Multiverse]] in a cataclysmic war lasting for eons and nearly destroying existence. To prevent this, the [[Time-Keepers]] brought peace and order to the Multiverse by arranging the timelines into a single "Sacred Timeline." In order to preserve the timeline's proper flow, the Time-Keepers then created the Time Variance Authority to police the Multiverse from Variants who create [[Observational Plane|Nexus]] events. If these events were left unchecked, the timeline could branch off and lead to another Multiversal War.{{Ref|LK101}} [[He Who Remains]] created this propaganda to give TVA workers purpose and dogma to cling to, and [[Miss Minutes]] helped spread it for centuries.{{Ref|LK106}}

===Arresting Loki===
{{Quote|On behalf of the Time Variance Authority, I hereby arrest you for your crimes against the Sacred Timeline.|[[Hunter B-15]] to [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]]|Glorious Purpose (Loki Season One)}}
In an [[2012/New York Time Heist|alternate version of 2012]], an alternate version of [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] was able to acquire the [[Tesseract]] and escape, eventually landing in the [[Gobi Desert]] in [[Mongolia]]. Seconds later, a Time Variance Authority unit led by [[Hunter B-15]] arrived and apprehended Loki for disrupting the Sacred Timeline before [[Reset Charge|pruning]] the alternate timeline. Loki was brought to the [[Time Variance Authority Office|TVA Office]] and went through a Variant process before he was brought into the TVA courtroom to stand in front of Judge [[Ravonna Renslayer]]. She asked Loki if he was guilty or not, to which he denied doing any crimes against the "Sacred Timeline". Loki then tried to use his powers, before he was told that magic doesn't work in the TVA. Renslayer sentenced Loki to be reset, but before he was taken away, he was saved by [[Mobius M. Mobius]] who convinced Renslayer that the TVA could use Loki to their advantage.{{Ref|LK101}}

====Recruiting Loki====
[[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] was recruited to work at the Time Variance Authority. [[Mobius M. Mobius]] instructed him to learn about the TVA and Loki worked at an office, where he read through TVA files and watched training videos. [[Miss Minutes]] tried to quiz Loki on what he learned, but was unsuccessful. Loki was then asked by Mobius to accompany him, [[Hunter B-15]], and other [[Minutemen]] on a mission. After causing the TVA to fail their mission, Loki was tasked by Mobius to go over each and every one of the Variant's case files. By reading a file on [[Ragnarök]], Loki figured out that the [[Sylvie Laufeydottir|Variant]] was hiding in apocalypses.{{Ref|LK102}}

===[[Bombing of the Sacred Timeline]]===
[[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]], [[Mobius M. Mobius]], [[Hunter B-15]], and other [[Minutemen]] went to [[Haven Hills]], [[Alabama]] in [[2050s#2050|2050]] to find the [[Sylvie Laufeydottir|Variant]]. During the mission, Loki met the Variant and was too late to stop her from setting off numerous [[Reset Charge]]s that fell through [[Timedoor]]s and landed at different points throughout the [[Sacred Timeline]]. However, the TVA was able to stabilize the Sacred Timeline by pruning the branched timelines.{{Ref|LK102}}

===The Truth Exposed===
Upon being taken to the [[Time-Keepers]]' chamber, [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] and [[Sylvie Laufeydottir|Sylvie]] [[Attack on the Time-Keepers|confronted]] the Time-Keepers. When Laufeydottir threw her sword at one of them, its head fell off, and the two discovered that the Time-Keepers were actually [[Glossary#Androids|androids]].{{Ref|LK104}}

===Death of the TVA's Creator===
====Opening of the Multiverse====
[[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] and [[Sylvie Laufeydottir|Sylvie]] enchanted [[Alioth]] in the [[Void (End of Time)|Void]], causing him to leave his post.{{Ref|LK105}} They then were able to access the [[Citadel at the End of Time]], where they were met by [[Miss Minutes]] and then [[He Who Remains]]. He Who Remains told Loki and Laufeydottir about his Variants, the [[Multiversal War]], and why he created the Time Variance Authority. He Who Remains offered them two options; kill him and risk starting a new Multiversal War or take over the Time Variance Authority. Loki wanted to think it through, but Laufeydottir, in a fit of revenge, pushed Loki through a [[Timedoor]] and killed He Who Remains. As soon as he died, dozens of branch timelines began to form.{{Ref|LK106}} This caused the TVA to start experiencing power surges.

Loki suddenly appeared in the TVA [[Time Variance Authority Office|office]] and found [[Casey]], relieved that Casey remembered him. He realized that he had previously been in the TVA's past and asked where [[Mobius M. Mobius]] and [[Hunter B-15]] were, but disappeared before Casey could take him to them. Casey approached Mobius and B-15 and told them what had happened, but they were interrupted by [[Hunter X-05]], who told them that the new [[Judges' Council]] wanted to see them in the War Room while Loki appeared and disappeared again in front of Casey.{{Ref|LK201}}

====End of Pruning====
In the War Room, the [[Judges' Council]] finished questioning [[Hunter D-90]] and brought in [[Hunter B-15]] and [[Mobius M. Mobius]], listening to a recording of [[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] telling Mobius the truth about him being a Variant. [[Gamble]] demanded the truth and [[Dox]] insisted they hold the meeting exactly according to protocol. B-15 managed to convince Gamble to end all pruning, effective immediately. Loki suddenly appeared in the War Room, using [[Hunter X-05]]'s [[Time Stick]] to reveal that the mural in the room of the [[Time-Keepers]] was covering a wall decoration depicting [[He Who Remains]]' face. Loki declared him to be the true creator of the TVA and that he would be returning.{{Ref|LK201}}

====Closing the Temporal Loom====
{{Quote|It looks like a disaster."<br>"It is a disaster.|[[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] and [[Ouroboros]]|Ouroboros (episode)}}
Mobius took Loki out of the room, and Loki explained that he was getting pulled between the past and present. Mobius brought Loki to [[Ouroboros]], who at first did not believe that Loki could be getting pulled between times, since the phenomenon, which he called "[[Time Slipping]]", was not possible within the [[Time Variance Authority Office]]. However, as Loki spoke to his past self, Ouroboros in the present realized that it was in fact possible and explained that Mobius needed to use a [[Temporal Aura Extractor]] to pull Loki out of the [[Temporal Loom]] while Loki pruned himself.

Loki returned to the present, when Ouroboros learned that the TVA had been experiencing power surges. As Mobius and Loki explained that they were allowing the timeline to branch now, Ouroboros realized that the branching was overloading the Temporal Loom, causing power surges. Once Ourboros' fears were confirmed, Loki asked how to stop the meltdown, and B-15 refused the option of pruning the branches. Ourboros told them the only other option was to close the blast doors to protect the TVA while he figured out how to retrofit the Temporal Loom to handle all of the branches.

Meanwhile, [[Dox]] started to raid the armory, and [[Hunter D-90]] rushed downstairs to tell B-15, Mobius, and Loki. B-15 left to handle Dox with D-90. Loki time slipped to the future while Ouroboros prepared Mobius. Mobius confronted the Temporal Loom and approached the device to attach the Aura Extractor. Mobius waited as long as he could before going back, and Ouroboros started to close the blast doors. Mobius nearly did not make it, but Loki was pulled through at the last moment and pushed them both inside. Loki then told Mobius that they needed to find [[Sylvie Laufeydottir]].{{Ref|LK201}}

====[[Attack on the Branching Timelines]]====
''To be added''{{Ref|LK202}}

====Evacuation====
{{Expand}}
Despite [[Ouroboros]]' efforts, the [[Temporal Loom]] overloaded and the [[Time Variance Authority Office]] was evacuated as Loki [[Time Slipping|time slipped]] into the future. Realizing he did not have a [[Time Stick]] to prune himself with, he rushed through the office, looking for one. The TVA lost significant power, and Loki ran out of time. He heard a phone ring and went to it, finding [[Sylvie Laufeydottir]] in an elevator before he got pruned{{Ref|LK201}} by his future self.{{Ref|LK204}}

===New Purpose===
====[[Liberation of the Multiverse]]====
[[Loki/New York Time Heist|Loki]] finally learned to control his [[Time Slipping]], traveling back initially in order to attempt to fix the [[Temporal Loom]] before realizing it was ultimately useless. Even when successful in enlarging the rings to allow for increased throughput, it was doomed to fail, given the infinite branching timelines. He eventually slipped back into the moment before [[Sylvie Laufeydottir]] killed [[He Who Remains]]. After numerous more failed attempts, he was finally told by He Who Remains the Loom was a failsafe to preserve the [[Sacred Timeline]]. With this new information, Loki finally knew his new purpose. Time slipping once more, he walked out the blast doors and used his powers to destroy the loom, grabbing timelines as he ascended. He finally sat down on the remains of the throne at the [[Citadel at the End of Time]], weaving the infinite branches together. The TVA switched to hunting the Variants of He Who Remains, while Mobius finally went to see [[Don|who he truly was]], observing himself playing with his sons.{{Ref|LK206}}

====Resistance from Mr. Paradox====
{{Expand}}
''To be added''{{Ref|DW}}

====Recruiting a Hero====
{{Quote|So, instead of deleting [[Hero of the Multiverse/Destiny Defying Multiverse Hero|you]] from all existence, we're gonna put you to work!"<br>"Uh..."<br>"Now, I don't need a hero, per se. What I need is an agent. You ready for a little more fun? Here we go!|[[Miss Minutes]] and [[Watcher]]|What If...? – An Immersive Story}}
A [[Hero of the Multiverse/Destiny Defying Multiverse Hero|Hero of the Multiverse]] chose to use the [[Infinity Stones]] to alter the fates of their allies. The TVA was alerted to the continuity error and sent [[Miss Minutes]] to handle the situation along with a desk and [[Chrono Monitor]]. There, she was confronted by the Hero and [[Watcher]]. She noted that timelines had been getting tangled, increasing continuity errors. Miss Minutes suggested that they should prune the branch, but the Watcher interrupted and explained that they were the Hero of the Multiverse. Miss Minutes then decided to recruit the Hero to the TVA, using the Chrono Monitor to introduce the Hero to [[Deadpool]], who she said would be the Hero's new coworker. Miss Minutes then used a [[Timedoor]] to take the hero to the [[Time Variance Authority Office]] so they could begin their training.{{Ref|WIAIS}}

====Theft of Reset Charges====
Members of the [[Guardians of the Multiverse]] came into contact with the TVA and stole several [[Reset Charge|reset charges]].{{Ref|WI307}}

